(4819236, 694343, 30861, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first blue. Lovely image.</td>', 'Congrats on your first blue. Lovely image.', '2008-07-11 13:33:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4819611, 694399, 3936, '<td valign="top">I think that this one comes across as more of an intersection, than an urban landscape.  <br/> <br/>The time lapse was done well.  But it is at street level, and there is one building to be seen.  <br/> <br/>I''m not sure what the blue lights are, but the one at the upper left competes with the rest of the image, and distracts the eye a bit.  Were this an advanced edtiting challenge, I would recommend cloning it out.<br/> <br/>The starbursts work well.  Focus is nice and sharp.  <br/> <br/>You might want to play with the white balance a bit.  The colors appear a little shifted.</td>', 'I think that this one comes across as more of an intersection, than an urban landscape.   The time lapse was done well.  But it is at street level, and there is one building to be seen.   I''m not sure what the blue lights are, but the one at the upper left competes with the rest of the image, and distracts the eye a bit.  Were this an advanced edtiting challenge, I would recommend cloning it out. The starbursts work well.  Focus is nice and sharp.   You might want to play with the white balance a bit.  The colors appear a little shifted.', '2008-07-11 17:13:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4819655, 693555, 66952, '<td valign="top">More than competent, especially since it was basic editing. I really like the off angle, it adds a lot of interest. I agree with whoever commented that the sky needs to be darker. A way to get this in basic is to darken the blues before doing the b&amp;w conversion.<br/> <br/>If it were me (take this with a grain of salt, my landscape abilities are caca), I would try two different things. First, I''d get down lower, closer to the water, then shoot up more to get more sky. I think that might be a more interesting angle. Second, I might try a long exposure, to make the water more silky smooth. That would require a ND filter or less light, maybe twilight. Or shoot very early in the morning when there''s less wind to disturb the water.</td>', 'More than competent, especially since it was basic editing. I really like the off angle, it adds a lot of interest. I agree with whoever commented that the sky needs to be darker. A way to get this in basic is to darken the blues before doing the b&w conversion. If it were me (take this with a grain of salt, my landscape abilities are caca), I would try two different things. First, I''d get down lower, closer to the water, then shoot up more to get more sky. I think that might be a more interesting angle. Second, I might try a long exposure, to make the water more silky smooth. That would require a ND filter or less light, maybe twilight. Or shoot very early in the morning when there''s less wind to disturb the water.', '2008-07-11 17:47:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4820077, 691939, 85102, '<td valign="top">damn, i thought this would have done better... :( i''m sorry. keep it up! once you get to know the ropes of the site, things will be swell!</td>', 'damn, i thought this would have done better... :( i''m sorry. keep it up! once you get to know the ropes of the site, things will be swell!', '2008-07-11 22:50:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4820101, 694399, 92601, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ambaker:</b></div><hr/><i> I think that this one comes across as more of an intersection, than an urban landscape.  <br/> <br/>The time lapse was done well.  But it is at street level, and there is one building to be seen.  <br/> <br/>I''m not sure what the blue lights are, but the one at the upper left competes with the rest of the image, and distracts the eye a bit.  Were this an advanced edtiting challenge, I would recommend cloning it out.<br/> <br/>The starbursts work well.  Focus is nice and sharp.  <br/> <br/>You might want to play with the white balance a bit.  The colors appear a little shifted. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the detailed comment. I actually did this an hour before the challenge was dude since i just wanted to turn anything in to see how it did. I walked about 5 mins to the intersection around my house and took a couple of exposures.<br/> <br/>This was taken in Daytona Beach, and theres not many buildings around here haha except for the beach and other private buildings like condos and stuff. I just thought that could represent the "urban life" even though this is more like a suburban.</td>', 'Originally posted by ambaker: I think that this one comes across as more of an intersection, than an urban landscape.   The time lapse was done well.  But it is at street level, and there is one building to be seen.   I''m not sure what the blue lights are, but the one at the upper left competes with the rest of the image, and distracts the eye a bit.  Were this an advanced edtiting challenge, I would recommend cloning it out. The starbursts work well.  Focus is nice and sharp.   You might want to play with the white balance a bit.  The colors appear a little shifted.   Thanks for the detailed comment. I actually did this an hour before the challenge was dude since i just wanted to turn anything in to see how it did. I walked about 5 mins to the intersection around my house and took a couple of exposures. This was taken in Daytona Beach, and theres not many buildings around here haha except for the beach and other private buildings like condos and stuff. I just thought that could represent the "urban life" even though this is more like a suburban.', '2008-07-11 23:18:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4821875, 694332, 51747, '<td valign="top">Awesome image! The color on Mt. Rainier really makes this picture a standout. Well done! I wish I had taken it. ( believe me I''ve tried!! lol)</td>', 'Awesome image! The color on Mt. Rainier really makes this picture a standout. Well done! I wish I had taken it. ( believe me I''ve tried!! lol)', '2008-07-13 12:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4822066, 694399, 52130, '<td valign="top">ooh very nice, I''ve never managed to get those really nice "starbursts" and red and blue really pop.</td>', 'ooh very nice, I''ve never managed to get those really nice "starbursts" and red and blue really pop.', '2008-07-13 15:19:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4824733, 693848, 30982, '<td valign="top">How did you keep the perspective so straight?  Great architecture shot.</td>', 'How did you keep the perspective so straight?  Great architecture shot.', '2008-07-14 17:12:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4824772, 693848, 56880, '<td valign="top">I was very careful to look straight up; no tripod that day.</td>', 'I was very careful to look straight up; no tripod that day.', '2008-07-14 17:25:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4825591, 694332, 47729, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Kerry Park is actually my favorite place to take pictures. <br/> <br/>Check out some other Seattle shots at <a href="//www.dpatterson.net/ViewGallery.aspx?gallery=Cityscape" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpatterson.net/ViewGallery.aspx?gallery=Cityscape</a> <br/> <br/>Once again - great job! The picture is superb!</td>', 'Great shot! Kerry Park is actually my favorite place to take pictures.  Check out some other Seattle shots at //www.dpatterson.net/ViewGallery.aspx?gallery=Cityscape  Once again - great job! The picture is superb!', '2008-07-15 02:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4827371, 693395, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Steve,<br/> <br/>        Nice image, There are two things in this image that are nicely done. The prospective of the building &amp; the play on the lighting are nice. What I do see here is and image thhat needed some sharpening in the horizontal &amp; vertical lines in the building itself. If you look closely you can see a jaggeredness in these lines. Secondly the light on the building is nice as I stated before but the sky (open) has a wide range of blue mergeing with the white at the bottom right. Here I think a better color balance was called for here &amp; would have improved the image overall. <br/></td>', 'Hi Steve,         Nice image, There are two things in this image that are nicely done. The prospective of the building & the play on the lighting are nice. What I do see here is and image thhat needed some sharpening in the horizontal & vertical lines in the building itself. If you look closely you can see a jaggeredness in these lines. Secondly the light on the building is nice as I stated before but the sky (open) has a wide range of blue mergeing with the white at the bottom right. Here I think a better color balance was called for here & would have improved the image overall. ', '2008-07-16 00:55:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4828882, 691917, 21189, '<td valign="top">*Camera envy*<br/> <br/>Nice photo - I do like the perspective from the other side of the river and the light trails. I noticed that all the urban landscapes feel a bit ''flat''. I think I''d have prefered diagonal leading lines for the buildings as opposed to having all the buildings pretty much lined up horizontally. Just a preferance thing I think.<br/> <br/>Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', '*Camera envy* Nice photo - I do like the perspective from the other side of the river and the light trails. I noticed that all the urban landscapes feel a bit ''flat''. I think I''d have prefered diagonal leading lines for the buildings as opposed to having all the buildings pretty much lined up horizontally. Just a preferance thing I think. Congrats on the ribbon!', '2008-07-16 13:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4828946, 694179, 67697, '<td valign="top">lol your work is soooo underappreciated.  I love how you framed the background buildings between the two stacks.  Very nice composition.</td>', 'lol your work is soooo underappreciated.  I love how you framed the background buildings between the two stacks.  Very nice composition.', '2008-07-16 13:20:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4830552, 693926, 89341, '<td valign="top">Just noticed your shutter and aperture settings, if you had used AV setting and f/16 or f/11 your shutter speed would still be around 1/100 or 1/200 and you would have got more dof (ie more focus through the shot)<br/> <br/>For every f-stop you change (bearing in mind your lens will change in 1/3 of a stop) you get twice (or half) as much light.<br/> <br/>So in your case f/5 @ 1/1000<br/>if you stop down 1 full f-stop to f/7.1 then you get half as much light and therefore you need a shutter speed of 1/500 for the correct exposure.</td>', 'Just noticed your shutter and aperture settings, if you had used AV setting and f/16 or f/11 your shutter speed would still be around 1/100 or 1/200 and you would have got more dof (ie more focus through the shot) For every f-stop you change (bearing in mind your lens will change in 1/3 of a stop) you get twice (or half) as much light. So in your case f/5 @ 1/1000if you stop down 1 full f-stop to f/7.1 then you get half as much light and therefore you need a shutter speed of 1/500 for the correct exposure.', '2008-07-17 06:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832191, 692822, 48954, '<td valign="top">6.7...damn who would have thought ;)</td>', '6.7...damn who would have thought ;)', '2008-07-18 08:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4832303, 692822, 67152, '<td valign="top">Great image - love the extreme distortion created by the fisheye.  That is one killer b/w conversion as well.</td>', 'Great image - love the extreme distortion created by the fisheye.  That is one killer b/w conversion as well.', '2008-07-18 11:33:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4837288, 692204, 30982, '<td valign="top">My kind of shot - I shoot from this perspective as often as I can find it.  Lots to see and explore, which as you know (and I persist on finding out over and over) is the kiss of death for scores around here.  To me, though, it makes for an interesting picture with more than 2 second appeal.</td>', 'My kind of shot - I shoot from this perspective as often as I can find it.  Lots to see and explore, which as you know (and I persist on finding out over and over) is the kiss of death for scores around here.  To me, though, it makes for an interesting picture with more than 2 second appeal.', '2008-07-21 17:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
